      <section id="security-risks">
        <h2>Cybersecurity Breakdown: Malware, Adware &amp; Phishing Risks</h2>
        <p>Because unauthorized media portals cannot monetize through standard digital ad networks like Google AdSense, they rely on high-risk third-party ad networks. This presents real cybersecurity hazards for unsuspecting visitors.</p>

        <ul>
          <li><strong>Drive-By APK File Prompts:</strong> Tapping anywhere on an unverified movie catalog page often triggers an unwanted pop-under tab that attempts to download a file named <code>Media_Player_Update.apk</code> or <code>Browser_Optimizer.apk</code>. Installing these unknown files can introduce keyloggers or spyware onto mobile devices.</li>
          <li><strong>Browser Push Notification Hijacking:</strong> Sites often employ deceptive CAPTCHA prompts stating <em>"Click Allow to prove you are not a robot"</em>. Once permitted, rogue ad servers flood the phone's notification bar with malicious ads and phishing links.</li>
          <li><strong>Malicious Redirection Loops:</strong> Users attempting to view movie information are frequently routed through multiple ad servers before reaching actual content, exposing their IP addresses to tracking scripts.</li>
        </ul>

        <p>To review official guidance on safe browsing and report malicious online portals, consult the <a href="https://cybercrime.gov.in/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color: var(--accent-cyan);">Indian Cyber Crime Reporting Portal</a>, which provides safety protocols maintained by the Ministry of Home Affairs.</p>
      </section>

